      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "This is a significant mismatch. The declared purpose lists 11+ broad PDF manipulation capabilities, but the actual code implements only a narrow subset focused on form field operations:\n\nIMPLEMENTED capabilities (with scripts):\n- Detecting fillable form fields (check_fillable_fields.py)\n- Extracting fillable form field information (extract_form_field_info.py)\n- Filling fillable PDF forms (fill_fillable_fields.py)\n- Creating form annotations to fill non-fillable PDFs (fill_pdf_form_with_annotations.py)\n- Extracting form structure from non-fillable PDFs (extract_form_structure.py)\n- Converting PDFs to images (convert_pdf_to_images.py)\n- Validating form field bounding boxes (check_bounding_boxes.py, create_validation_image.py)\n\nMISSING capabilities with NO implementation:\n1. Reading/extracting general text content (no script for this)\n2. Extracting tables from PDFs (no script for this)\n3. Merging/combining multiple PDFs (no script for this)\n4. Splitting PDFs (no script for this)\n5. Rotating PDF pages (no script for this)\n6. Adding watermarks (no script for this)\n7. Creating new PDFs from scratch (no script for this)\n8. Encrypting PDFs (no script for this)\n9. Decrypting PDFs (no script for this)\n10. Extracting images from PDFs (no script for this)\n11. OCR on scanned PDFs (no script for this)\n\nThe description overstates capabilities by roughly 3x. A user expecting to merge PDFs, add watermarks, or perform OCR would be unable to do so with this skill. The actual implementation is valid and well-designed for form field operations, but significantly underdelivers on the declared scope.",
      "remediation": "Update the skill description to accurately reflect all capabilities, or remove undeclared functionality from the implementation.",
      "code_snippet": null,
      "intent": null,
      "tags": [
        "ASI02",
        "AML.T0080",
        "llm-unconfirmed"
      ]
