      "explanation": "The documentation instructs users to create and modify PDF files without explicit warnings about the potential for malicious use or unauthorized document manipulation. An attacker could exploit this skill to programmatically create fraudulent forms, modify existing PDFs to commit document forgery, or generate deceptive content at scale. The lack of explicit user warnings about these risks enables misuse.",
      "remediation": "Add prominent warnings in the documentation about responsible use, including: (1) A security notice at the top of the file warning users that PDF form filling and manipulation should only be performed on documents they own or have explicit permission to modify; (2) Explicit guidance that this skill should not be used for creating fraudulent documents, forging signatures, or any unauthorized modifications; (3) Clear examples of what constitutes misuse (e.g., modifying legal documents without authorization, creating counterfeit forms); (4) Recommend audit logging or user confirmation steps when filling sensitive forms.",
      "code_snippet": null,
