      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "The file write operation at line 21 (image.save()) writes images directly to disk without any user confirmation, warning, or validation of the output directory. An attacker could exploit this by manipulating the output_dir parameter to write files to sensitive system locations, overwrite existing files, or fill up disk space. Since this is called from user-supplied command-line arguments without path validation, it creates an arbitrary file write vulnerability.",
      "remediation": "Implement the following controls: (1) Validate the output directory path to ensure it's within an expected safe directory using os.path.abspath() and path normalization; (2) Check if the output directory exists and is writable before attempting writes; (3) Add user confirmation before writing files, especially if the output directory is not explicitly trusted; (4) Implement file path validation to prevent directory traversal attacks (reject paths containing '..' or absolute paths outside allowed directories); (5) Add checks to prevent overwriting existing files without explicit user consent; (6) Consider implementing disk space checks to prevent disk exhaustion attacks.",
